From 6f84e19996e94ca40097f900ee8a6d6d354a2634 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:11:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] nvk: prepare for an nvkmd backend that is not DRM

Split nvk_create_drm_physical_device() so that the part which turns an
nvkmd_pdev into an nvk_physical_device can be reused, and add an
instance-level enumerate hook backed by nvkmd_enumerate_non_drm_pdevs().
When that returns VK_ERROR_INCOMPATIBLE_DRIVER (always, for now) the
common code falls back to DRM enumeration exactly as before.

Also:
 - only install vk_drm_syncobj_copy_payloads when the nvkmd device has a
   DRM fd,
 - advertise the fd/dma-buf external memory, semaphore and fence
   extensions only when nvkmd_info::has_dma_buf is set, and use a
   software WSI device (CPU copy on present) when it is not,
 - add nvkmd_info::has_host_visible_vram and only expose the
   DEVICE_LOCAL|HOST_VISIBLE memory type when it is set,
 - export nouveau_ws_device_info_init_limits() from the winsys so that a
   backend which only knows the chipset can fill in the SM version and
   per-SM limits the same way nouveau does.

nouveau sets has_dma_buf and has_host_visible_vram, so there is no
functional change for nouveau.

